WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:11.972 --> 00:00:14.766
-Hello.
-Hi, Bridget. Sorry, I'm late.

2
00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:17.769
You know the only thing better
than a patient being late

3
00:00:17.852 --> 00:00:19.187
is one who doesn't turn up at all.

4
00:00:21.064 --> 00:00:22.232
So where did we leave off?

5
00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:26.319
Let's see.
I have it in my notes-- Oh, yeah!

6
00:00:26.403 --> 00:00:28.989
"Ted Lasso is driving me fucking crazy."

7
00:00:29.072 --> 00:00:31.408
All right. He refuses to open up.

8
00:00:31.491 --> 00:00:33.910
And when he gets anywhere close
to being vulnerable,

9
00:00:33.994 --> 00:00:38.290
he fires off a zinger or some obscure
reference to something very specific

10
00:00:38.373 --> 00:00:40.709
to a 40-year-old white man
from middle America.

11
00:00:40.792 --> 00:00:43.253
So he's refusing
to be vulnerable, right?

12
00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:45.088
Sounds like someone I know.

13
00:00:45.171 --> 00:00:47.799
Oh, stop it.
Me and Coach Lasso are nothing alike.

14
00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:50.010
Sharon, you do the same thing.

15
00:00:50.093 --> 00:00:54.014
He uses humor to deflect,
you use your intelligence.

16
00:00:54.097 --> 00:00:55.307
Please.

17
00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.768
I do not harness my savantish nature
to alienate people and isolate myself.

18
00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:01.396
Okay, I hear that.

19
00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:04.106
I doubt you'll make any headway
with Coach Lasso

20
00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:07.444
until you let your guard down yourself
and meet him halfway.

21
00:01:08.028 --> 00:01:09.029
You're right.

22
00:01:09.112 --> 00:01:11.364
Of course, I'm right!
Now, what are you going to do?

23
00:01:28.882 --> 00:01:30.926
-Mind your dog!
-What?

24
00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:32.510
-He hates that sweater.
-Up yours!

25
00:01:38.225 --> 00:01:39.643
Shit!

26
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:49.277
Call 999. Someone call 999.

27
00:02:23.061 --> 00:02:24.062
Hi, guys.

28
00:02:26.356 --> 00:02:30.151
So, I actually have a fun,
new branding opportunity for a coach.

29
00:02:30.235 --> 00:02:32.529
It's only one public appearance.
It's decent money.

30
00:02:32.612 --> 00:02:34.573
Would be really good for the club.

31
00:02:34.656 --> 00:02:36.783
Would either one of you want
to help me out

32
00:02:36.866 --> 00:02:39.327
by being a spokesperson for this--

33
00:02:42.831 --> 00:02:45.125
Right. Fuck you both.

34
00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.087
I respect that we didn't
have to say a word.

35
00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.255
She gets us.

36
00:02:51.423 --> 00:02:53.258
I'm going to be a spokesperson.

37
00:02:54.551 --> 00:02:55.552
Where's Ted?

38
00:02:56.136 --> 00:02:58.722
-He texted. He has some emergency.
-What?

39
00:02:58.805 --> 00:03:00.765
-I didn't ask.
-Why not?

40
00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:02.183
It's his emergency.

41
00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:03.852
If he wanted him to know,
he would have said.

42
00:03:04.978 --> 00:03:08.023
We have an FA Cup semifinal
at Wembley Stadium on Sunday.

43
00:03:08.106 --> 00:03:09.816
-Who's running training?
-Me.

44
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.569
-You?
-Ted asked. I don't give a shit.

45
00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:17.741
-Shit, I got to go.
-Where you going?

46
00:03:17.824 --> 00:03:19.492
None of your fucking business.

47
00:03:25.415 --> 00:03:28.251
Well…
Guess that just leaves us two. I mean--

48
00:03:28.335 --> 00:03:29.836
-You can run training.
-Thank you.

49
00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.214
That will be great-- I think--
Yes, thank you. Hold on.

50
00:03:42.682 --> 00:03:44.684
All right, man. Let's go.

51
00:03:45.268 --> 00:03:48.021
Switch it on, boy.
Yeah, let's go, let's go.

52
00:03:48.104 --> 00:03:49.689
Good man. All you, mate.

53
00:03:49.773 --> 00:03:51.733
That's it, you got it,
you got it, you got it.

54
00:03:52.275 --> 00:03:53.276
Hello, Daddy.

55
00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.029
Sam…
Do you know why I'm calling?

56
00:03:56.655 --> 00:03:57.864
No, sir.

57
00:03:57.948 --> 00:03:59.741
I'm calling because Cerithium Oil

58
00:03:59.824 --> 00:04:02.786
has just been ordered
to stop operating in Nigeria.

59
00:04:02.869 --> 00:04:05.622
Wait, what? Wait, that's incredible!

60
00:04:05.705 --> 00:04:08.833
And you were the butterfly
whose wings made this happen.

61
00:04:08.917 --> 00:04:10.669
I'm so proud of you, my son.

62
00:04:10.752 --> 00:04:12.045
Thank you, Dad.

63
00:04:12.128 --> 00:04:14.548
I mean, look, I only did it
because you inspired me to.

64
00:04:14.631 --> 00:04:18.425
I appreciate you saying that,
because it's absolutely true.

65
00:04:19.803 --> 00:04:20.804
I love you.

66
00:04:20.887 --> 00:04:23.098
I love you too. Okay, bye-bye.

67
00:04:23.932 --> 00:04:25.559
Oi! What you doing?

68
00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:27.185
Oh, shit.

69
00:04:28.937 --> 00:04:31.314
-Why didn't you say anything?
-It was on my neck.

70
00:04:32.482 --> 00:04:33.567
Yeah. Sorry.

71
00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:35.652
You know what, sod off.
I got this.

72
00:04:46.955 --> 00:04:48.707
I haven't found a term I like yet

73
00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.792
for when I tell people I'm taking a shit.

74
00:04:51.626 --> 00:04:52.794
What do you use?

75
00:04:55.171 --> 00:04:57.090
I need to reapply my lip liner.

76
00:04:58.049 --> 00:04:59.050
Men don't know what that means

77
00:04:59.134 --> 00:05:01.177
and women understand
it requires time and focus.

78
00:05:09.394 --> 00:05:10.854
Say fucking yes!

79
00:05:14.733 --> 00:05:17.444
Guys, guys! Three dots!
Three dots, three dots.

80
00:05:24.034 --> 00:05:25.243
Yes!

81
00:05:28.496 --> 00:05:29.915
Yeah!

82
00:05:29.998 --> 00:05:31.917
-Wow. Oh, my God.
-Yes!

83
00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:34.961
Captain.

84
00:05:35.587 --> 00:05:36.588
Yeah, bruv?

85
00:05:36.671 --> 00:05:38.632
I would like to ask you for a haircut.

86
00:05:38.715 --> 00:05:39.883
What?

87
00:05:44.429 --> 00:05:45.472
Are you sure, bruv?

88
00:05:45.555 --> 00:05:47.015
Yes, I think I am.

89
00:05:53.188 --> 00:05:55.690
All right. After training.

90
00:05:58.902 --> 00:06:00.654
-Isaac, Isaac.
-Oh, shit!

91
00:06:04.532 --> 00:06:05.533
Oh, now hold on, lady.

92
00:06:05.617 --> 00:06:07.869
You're telling me
I could shatter every bone in my body,

93
00:06:07.953 --> 00:06:10.413
someone could just drop me off
in front of any old hospital,

94
00:06:10.497 --> 00:06:12.040
dumped into a garbage can or something,

95
00:06:12.123 --> 00:06:14.709
and y'all patch me up
and I don't have to pay jack squat?

96
00:06:14.793 --> 00:06:16.211
You're damn right.

97
00:06:16.294 --> 00:06:18.046
I tell you, I love this country.
I love this town.

98
00:06:18.129 --> 00:06:22.050
Oh, did you know that Winnie the Pooh was
based on a real bear from the London Zoo?

99
00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:23.301
Fuck me.

100
00:06:24.386 --> 00:06:25.637
Oh, no…

101
00:06:26.471 --> 00:06:27.847
It's worse than I imagined.

102
00:06:31.309 --> 00:06:32.561
She can walk again!

103
00:06:33.687 --> 00:06:35.063
It's a miracle!

104
00:06:35.146 --> 00:06:37.065
Oh, thank God for science!

105
00:06:37.941 --> 00:06:40.235
Hey, Doc! The doc going to be okay, Doc?

106
00:06:40.318 --> 00:06:41.486
Yes, her scan seemed fine.

107
00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:43.321
Good. No intracranial hemorrhaging?

108
00:06:43.405 --> 00:06:45.824
-No.
-Or subdural hematoma?

109
00:06:45.907 --> 00:06:47.951
No. You seem to know
a lot about brain injuries.

110
00:06:48.034 --> 00:06:50.537
Well, I watched
a lot of Grey's Anatomy in my early 30s.

111
00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.248
And actually, you know,
I coached football.

112
00:06:53.331 --> 00:06:54.916
The American kind. You know?

113
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.836
The one with all the concussions
and hullabaloo about kneeling and such.

114
00:06:57.919 --> 00:06:59.796
Oh, well, she does have a concussion.

115
00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.965
And she's had a couple stitches
in her head.

116
00:07:02.048 --> 00:07:04.342
So you'll need to rest
for a few days, okay?

117
00:07:04.426 --> 00:07:06.595
Apart from that,
your husband can take you home.

118
00:07:06.678 --> 00:07:08.013
Oh, he's not my husband.

119
00:07:08.096 --> 00:07:10.390
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Ain't no ring on these fingers.

120
00:07:10.473 --> 00:07:11.975
-No, we're just friends.
-Colleagues.

121
00:07:12.058 --> 00:07:14.352
-Friendly colleagues.
-I don't have a husband.

122
00:07:14.436 --> 00:07:15.437
Yeah, but not in a sad way.

123
00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.564
You know, she's just fiercely independent.

124
00:07:17.647 --> 00:07:20.066
And I'm perfectly capable
of taking myself home.

125
00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.777
-See what I mean?
-I'm sorry, Dr. Fieldstone.

126
00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.113
Hospital policy states
that head trauma patients,

127
00:07:25.196 --> 00:07:26.364
they cannot leave unattended.

128
00:07:27.282 --> 00:07:28.950
And there ain't no policy
like a hospital policy,

129
00:07:29.034 --> 00:07:30.827
'cause a hospital policy don't stop.

130
00:07:31.453 --> 00:07:32.704
Let me help you out with that, sweetheart.

131
00:07:32.787 --> 00:07:34.915
-Here you go. There you go.
-Thank you.

132
00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.709
Thank you for being here, Coach Kent.

133
00:07:38.293 --> 00:07:40.879
My sister's at the hospital.
She works in the emergency room.

134
00:07:41.421 --> 00:07:43.465
She can't really pop out
'cause there's always someone coming in

135
00:07:43.548 --> 00:07:47.844
with, like, a knife stuck in their eye
or a torch stuck up their--

136
00:07:47.928 --> 00:07:49.679
Yeah, okay, I get it. She's busy.

137
00:07:50.639 --> 00:07:53.767
Phoebe, would you mind doing some coloring
while I talk to your uncle?

138
00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.435
Yes, Ms. Bowen.

139
00:07:59.272 --> 00:08:01.316
Can I start with
a quick personal question?

140
00:08:01.399 --> 00:08:03.485
-Phoebe's dad--
-Oh, he's a piece of shit.

141
00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:07.280
-Is he alive?
-Sorry, yeah. He's a living piece of shit.

142
00:08:08.156 --> 00:08:09.366
Right.

143
00:08:09.449 --> 00:08:13.161
Well, Coach Kent, we've got a bit of
an issue with Phoebe's behavior.

144
00:08:17.082 --> 00:08:20.335
-Let's have it.
-She's been swearing. A lot.

145
00:08:20.418 --> 00:08:21.503
How bad is it?

146
00:08:21.586 --> 00:08:25.924
Today she called one of her classmates
an "apathetic shitfucker."

147
00:08:26.508 --> 00:08:28.093
-Are they?
-Oh, yes.

148
00:08:28.677 --> 00:08:29.928
But that's not the point.

149
00:08:31.388 --> 00:08:33.765
Do you have any idea
where she might be getting this from?

150
00:08:39.395 --> 00:08:40.647
Me?

151
00:08:43.024 --> 00:08:46.027
Fuck.

152
00:08:46.111 --> 00:08:49.864
This was her fifth offense.
She got warnings, then isolation.

153
00:08:49.948 --> 00:08:52.492
Now I'm afraid she has to go home
for the rest of the day.

154
00:08:53.118 --> 00:08:54.828
You know the influence you have on her.

155
00:08:55.412 --> 00:08:56.413
Use it.

156
00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.874
Oi!

157
00:08:59.958 --> 00:09:00.959
We're leaving.

158
00:09:05.213 --> 00:09:07.173
Sorry for what I said, Ms. Bowen.

159
00:09:07.257 --> 00:09:08.800
Thank you, Phoebe.

160
00:09:09.551 --> 00:09:11.177
Uncle Roy, can we get ice cream?

161
00:09:11.761 --> 00:09:12.762
Fuck no!

162
00:09:14.514 --> 00:09:15.724
Sorry.

163
00:09:17.434 --> 00:09:18.643
F-no!

164
00:09:20.937 --> 00:09:23.148
Go on, scoot your boot.

165
00:09:31.281 --> 00:09:32.991
Fucking glitter.

166
00:09:34.576 --> 00:09:37.329
By all measures,
it's not the cruelest prank ever played,

167
00:09:37.412 --> 00:09:40.040
but no one should ever make someone
eat a Vaseline sandwich.

168
00:09:40.123 --> 00:09:41.833
But that's Ronnie Fouch for you.

169
00:09:41.917 --> 00:09:42.918
Innovator.

170
00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.295
How did you know I was in the hospital?

171
00:09:45.378 --> 00:09:48.590
Oh, you left me a bunch of voice notes.
Yeah, 32 to be exact.

172
00:09:49.174 --> 00:09:52.802
-I thought those deleted themselves.
-Yeah, well, I kept all those puppies.

173
00:09:52.886 --> 00:09:54.846
You should listen to some of these.
They are a hoot.

174
00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:57.724
-Please, no, thank you.
-It doesn't matter. I got them right here.

175
00:09:57.807 --> 00:10:01.436
Ted, it's Sharon.
I can't come to the phone right now.

176
00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:04.522
But if you want to talk my ear off
about some bullshit

177
00:10:04.606 --> 00:10:08.235
because you're too afraid
to properly emote, leave a message.

178
00:10:08.318 --> 00:10:10.111
Beep!

179
00:10:10.195 --> 00:10:13.031
-I didn't mean it.
-Come on now. You meant it a little bit.

180
00:10:13.114 --> 00:10:16.868
In concussio veritas, right?
Ain't that the saying?

181
00:10:16.952 --> 00:10:20.121
This next one brings
Mr. Stephen Sondheim in the house

182
00:10:20.205 --> 00:10:22.249
'cause it's you singing "Tonight"
from West Side Story,

183
00:10:22.332 --> 00:10:25.627
but doing both the parts of
Tony and Maria at the same time,

184
00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:28.046
which is, well, in a word, thrilling.
Here it is.

185
00:10:28.129 --> 00:10:29.381
Tonight, tonight

186
00:10:30.924 --> 00:10:31.925
Feel that.

187
00:10:32.008 --> 00:10:34.261
And you do the whole first act.
It's incredible.

188
00:11:07.502 --> 00:11:09.045
What is the big deal?

189
00:11:10.255 --> 00:11:11.590
Not now.

190
00:11:11.673 --> 00:11:14.426
My guy,
Isaac's an artist with those clippers.

191
00:11:14.509 --> 00:11:16.761
But he only gives you
one haircut per season,

192
00:11:16.845 --> 00:11:19.222
so you try and save that
for a very special occasion.

193
00:11:19.306 --> 00:11:21.016
I'm not using mine until I marry.

194
00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.226
Or I get circumcised.

195
00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:24.436
Quite right.

196
00:11:24.519 --> 00:11:27.063
Bro, I can't believe you're wasting
your Isaac cut on a blind date.

197
00:11:27.147 --> 00:11:29.858
Yeah. What if you and this babes
only got textual chemistry?

198
00:11:29.941 --> 00:11:30.942
Guys…

199
00:11:32.068 --> 00:11:33.069
I believe…

200
00:11:34.946 --> 00:11:36.573
this could be
something very special.

201
00:11:44.331 --> 00:11:45.665
So do we all just stand here--

202
00:11:45.749 --> 00:11:47.709
Oh, my God!

203
00:11:48.293 --> 00:11:50.545
Shut the fuck up, Jan Maas.

204
00:11:52.214 --> 00:11:53.215
Sorry.

205
00:12:01.139 --> 00:12:02.724
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

206
00:12:02.807 --> 00:12:04.017
It's like Swan Lake.

207
00:12:38.885 --> 00:12:41.596
Oh! Yeah!

208
00:13:05.704 --> 00:13:06.705
Come in!

209
00:13:11.293 --> 00:13:12.294
Hi.

210
00:13:14.462 --> 00:13:15.463
What's this about?

211
00:13:16.047 --> 00:13:18.842
I'm just in here until my office exists.

212
00:13:19.342 --> 00:13:20.760
It's really no problem.

213
00:13:20.844 --> 00:13:24.222
If I spill anything,
I'm next to everything I need to clean up.

214
00:13:24.848 --> 00:13:25.974
This is very, very sad.

215
00:13:26.057 --> 00:13:28.351
What can I do for you, Jamie?

216
00:13:29.603 --> 00:13:32.439
Can I get me dad and his two mates
on the list for Wembley tickets, please?

217
00:13:32.522 --> 00:13:35.859
Of course! Family section? VIP?

218
00:13:35.942 --> 00:13:37.944
Put 'em in the car park for all I care.

219
00:13:38.028 --> 00:13:39.905
Just getting him tickets
so he'll get off me back.

220
00:13:40.614 --> 00:13:41.865
Fathers and sons.

221
00:13:41.948 --> 00:13:43.408
So tricky.

222
00:13:43.491 --> 00:13:45.702
They should really write songs about it.

223
00:13:46.703 --> 00:13:49.122
-Think they do.
-Yeah, I know. I was just--

224
00:13:50.415 --> 00:13:51.666
Anyway…

225
00:13:53.251 --> 00:13:56.504
You… Are you close with your dad?

226
00:13:57.005 --> 00:13:59.591
Ups and downs, like everyone.

227
00:13:59.674 --> 00:14:01.009
It's complicated.

228
00:14:01.092 --> 00:14:03.303
Mine's not complicated. He's just a dick.

229
00:14:03.386 --> 00:14:06.056
Every situation,
he does exactly what a dick would do.

230
00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:08.475
Not much you can do with that.
Know what I mean?

231
00:14:08.558 --> 00:14:12.771
Well, I try to love my dad for who he is
and forgive him for who he isn't.

232
00:14:14.898 --> 00:14:20.320
Look, Jamie. Whatever he may be,
he's your father, which makes him a VIP.

233
00:14:21.655 --> 00:14:22.989
Names?

234
00:14:23.073 --> 00:14:24.532
James Tartt.

235
00:14:26.576 --> 00:14:30.789
His mates are Denbo Cullens and Bug.

236
00:14:31.873 --> 00:14:34.709
-"Bug"?
-Just Bug. One G.

237
00:14:34.793 --> 00:14:35.961
Like the animal.

238
00:14:36.503 --> 00:14:37.963
It's his legal name. Changed it.

239
00:14:38.046 --> 00:14:40.048
Because he's small like a bug?

240
00:14:40.131 --> 00:14:41.758
No, 'cause he eats bugs for money.

241
00:14:42.259 --> 00:14:43.260
Right.

242
00:14:45.178 --> 00:14:46.388
Thanks for that.

243
00:14:46.471 --> 00:14:47.556
Yeah.

244
00:14:47.639 --> 00:14:48.640
Okay.

245
00:14:49.432 --> 00:14:50.475
Open or closed?

246
00:14:51.476 --> 00:14:52.602
Closed.

247
00:14:52.686 --> 00:14:53.853
You get less questions.

248
00:14:54.813 --> 00:14:56.439
-All right.
-Bye.

249
00:15:02.946 --> 00:15:04.656
Thank you for the ice cream, Uncle Roy.

250
00:15:05.699 --> 00:15:06.950
Oi!

251
00:15:13.331 --> 00:15:14.874
You can't swear, Phoebe.

252
00:15:15.458 --> 00:15:16.960
But you swear all the time.

253
00:15:17.043 --> 00:15:18.128
Yeah.

254
00:15:18.211 --> 00:15:21.590
And it didn't hold me back
'cause I'm a footballer.

255
00:15:21.673 --> 00:15:25.135
No one cares if we swear.
It's part of the job. It's encouraged.

256
00:15:26.595 --> 00:15:30.140
But you can't be a doctor,
or a teacher, or a--

257
00:15:30.223 --> 00:15:32.309
Veterinarian for wild animals.

258
00:15:32.392 --> 00:15:35.228
Or a veterinarian for wild animals.
I still don't get how that works.

259
00:15:35.312 --> 00:15:37.063
You treat them in the woods
and no one pays you?

260
00:15:37.147 --> 00:15:38.148
It doesn't matter.

261
00:15:38.231 --> 00:15:42.903
The point is you can't do that
if you swear all the time.

262
00:15:46.239 --> 00:15:49.534
Look. You and I spend
a lot of time together,

263
00:15:50.118 --> 00:15:51.536
and I love every second.

264
00:15:53.705 --> 00:15:56.124
I weren't trained
in how to be around a kid.

265
00:15:58.084 --> 00:15:59.669
And sometimes…

266
00:16:00.921 --> 00:16:02.547
I get concerned…

267
00:16:05.508 --> 00:16:10.430
that I've been infecting you
with the worst parts of me.

268
00:16:11.014 --> 00:16:12.724
That's not true.

269
00:16:13.558 --> 00:16:16.311
Uncle Roy, you teach me great things.

270
00:16:17.187 --> 00:16:19.648
I called that boy a name
because he's a bully.

271
00:16:19.731 --> 00:16:22.651
And because of you, I stand up to bullies.

272
00:16:25.737 --> 00:16:26.738
And referees.

273
00:16:29.407 --> 00:16:31.284
And I can do that without swearing.

274
00:16:31.993 --> 00:16:32.994
Yeah.

275
00:16:33.828 --> 00:16:35.372
'Cause you are better than me.

276
00:16:36.164 --> 00:16:37.707
I'm as good as the best you.

277
00:16:39.292 --> 00:16:41.461
Maybe we can stop swearing together.

278
00:16:41.545 --> 00:16:42.921
Fuck you.

279
00:16:44.339 --> 00:16:45.340
I can't.

280
00:16:46.216 --> 00:16:47.217
But you can.

281
00:16:49.719 --> 00:16:51.012
Pretty please.

282
00:16:51.096 --> 00:16:52.514
Okay, Uncle Roy.

283
00:16:53.348 --> 00:16:55.559
Good. Now get out of here.

284
00:16:55.642 --> 00:16:59.062
Can you come in
for one game of Princess and Dragon?

285
00:16:59.646 --> 00:17:01.273
Can I be the dragon this time?

286
00:17:01.356 --> 00:17:02.774
No.

287
00:17:02.857 --> 00:17:05.068
Fine. But you better have fixed the wand.

288
00:17:09.197 --> 00:17:11.408
All right. Tight squeeze, huh?

289
00:17:11.491 --> 00:17:13.910
Probably a little bit easier
when this thing can fold up, I bet.

290
00:17:13.994 --> 00:17:16.246
Thank you for walking me home.
I'm good from here.

291
00:17:16.329 --> 00:17:18.497
Well, that's the fifth time
you've said that.

292
00:17:18.582 --> 00:17:20.917
I'll just set this puppy down
and I'll skedaddle.

293
00:17:21.626 --> 00:17:23.420
Yeah, there you go.

294
00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.214
Good spot for it. There you go.

295
00:17:31.845 --> 00:17:32.971
Corporate housing, huh?

296
00:17:33.054 --> 00:17:34.848
It does not disappoint, does it?

297
00:17:34.931 --> 00:17:37.809
It don't really do anything.
I guess that's part of the idea, ain't it?

298
00:17:37.893 --> 00:17:39.853
What we got back here? Hey.

299
00:17:40.812 --> 00:17:43.189
All right. Home entertainment center.

300
00:17:44.024 --> 00:17:47.986
Well, you know what,
I'll just say that it's fine and move on.

301
00:17:48.069 --> 00:17:49.362
It's temporary.

302
00:17:49.446 --> 00:17:51.573
Yeah, well, you know, what isn't, right?

303
00:17:53.074 --> 00:17:54.743
-Would you like some tea?
-Oh, hell no.

304
00:17:55.452 --> 00:17:59.456
No, I mean no, thank you.
Sorry, just don't care for that garbage.

305
00:17:59.539 --> 00:18:00.999
I have water and I have wine.

306
00:18:01.082 --> 00:18:03.126
Chicken and the egg, huh? Yeah.

307
00:18:03.209 --> 00:18:05.253
I'll take some water.
That'd be great. Thanks.

308
00:18:06.046 --> 00:18:07.047
Tap okay?

309
00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:11.259
Oh, yeah. No, I like my water
like Kyrie Irving likes his Earth. Flat.

310
00:18:18.141 --> 00:18:21.978
So, you gonna get a new bike,
or you wanna lay off riding for a bit?

311
00:18:22.062 --> 00:18:23.939
I don't know. I haven't thought about it.

312
00:18:24.022 --> 00:18:27.442
Well, I hope you get back on that horse.
And by horse, I mean bicycle.

313
00:18:27.525 --> 00:18:30.612
Although how cool would it be
if you started riding a horse to work?

314
00:18:30.695 --> 00:18:32.530
Everybody starts calling you
"Dr. Sharon Horsewoman" or--

315
00:18:32.614 --> 00:18:33.907
You know, becomes your hook.

316
00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:35.784
I really should get some rest.

317
00:18:35.867 --> 00:18:38.954
Hey, 10-4, good buddy. Good colleague.

318
00:18:58.014 --> 00:18:59.349
Delicious as always.

319
00:19:01.851 --> 00:19:04.604
Yeah, all right, no,
I'll let you go here, and--

320
00:19:04.688 --> 00:19:06.815
You just give me a holler
if you need anything.

321
00:19:06.898 --> 00:19:08.733
You know, you had quite the scare today.

322
00:19:08.817 --> 00:19:12.404
And my job is teaching people
how to overcome what happened to me.

323
00:19:12.487 --> 00:19:13.822
I'm fine, thank you.

324
00:19:13.905 --> 00:19:15.115
Goodbye, Coach Lasso.

325
00:19:17.867 --> 00:19:19.703
Yeah, all right now, Doc. Take care.

326
00:19:41.474 --> 00:19:42.934
Jesus! Hello.

327
00:19:44.269 --> 00:19:46.021
Why are you picking up right now?

328
00:19:46.104 --> 00:19:47.689
You were supposed to be in there
five minutes ago.

329
00:19:47.772 --> 00:19:49.649
Right. I can't go in.

330
00:19:49.733 --> 00:19:52.444
Oh, come on.
You've got this. Get in there.

331
00:19:52.527 --> 00:19:54.613
Either it's gonna be
the most amazing night

332
00:19:54.696 --> 00:19:55.989
or it's gonna be so shit

333
00:19:56.072 --> 00:19:58.825
that you can punish me for it
for the rest of our friendship.

334
00:19:59.451 --> 00:20:00.827
I do like the sound of that.

335
00:20:00.911 --> 00:20:03.121
I'm gonna hang up
'cause you're gonna go, yeah?

336
00:20:04.205 --> 00:20:06.958
You look so beautiful I can't bear it.

337
00:20:19.596 --> 00:20:21.890
Ms. Welton. Rebecca.

338
00:20:22.432 --> 00:20:23.433
Sam!

339
00:20:23.516 --> 00:20:26.811
-Hi. Hello.
-Well, that's a coincidence.

340
00:20:29.314 --> 00:20:30.315
What's-- What's wrong?

341
00:20:30.398 --> 00:20:32.525
What? Oh, God. Yeah, I'm fi-- I'm just--

342
00:20:32.609 --> 00:20:36.738
I'm just a little bit nervous
'cause I'm meeting someone.

343
00:20:36.821 --> 00:20:38.198
Okay, well, I--

344
00:20:38.281 --> 00:20:43.245
Don't be nervous,
'cause you look stunning as always.

345
00:20:43.745 --> 00:20:45.121
Thank you, Sam.

346
00:20:45.205 --> 00:20:47.540
Oh, God, don't let me
get in the way of--

347
00:20:47.624 --> 00:20:50.085
-You have a lovely evening.
-Yes. Thank you. You too.

348
00:20:50.168 --> 00:20:51.211
Great haircut.

349
00:20:51.294 --> 00:20:53.964
-Oh. Well, thank you.
-Yes.

350
00:20:54.047 --> 00:20:55.465
That's just weird.

351
00:21:12.482 --> 00:21:13.483
Keeley says hi.

352
00:21:14.109 --> 00:21:16.361
Oh… tell her I say hello.

353
00:21:37.465 --> 00:21:38.675
Oh, shit!

354
00:21:38.758 --> 00:21:39.885
-What?
-Shit.

355
00:21:39.968 --> 00:21:40.927
-What?
-Shit.

356
00:21:41.011 --> 00:21:43.305
-What? What? What?
-Shit. God, this can't be happening!

357
00:21:43.388 --> 00:21:46.308
-But it is. It's--
-I knew I shouldn't have come in here.

358
00:21:46.391 --> 00:21:48.894
-But you did. You d--
-No. Sam.

359
00:21:50.145 --> 00:21:51.897
We can't-- I'm your boss.

360
00:21:53.106 --> 00:21:57.652
No. No. You are way too young.
I mean, you're what, like, 24?

361
00:21:57.736 --> 00:22:00.238
-I'm-- I'm 21.
-Oh, my God. I'm a pedophile.

362
00:22:00.322 --> 00:22:03.366
I feel-- I've groomed you.
All these messages. I was grooming you!

363
00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:06.077
You didn't groom me, okay?
We didn't know who we were.

364
00:22:06.161 --> 00:22:09.581
Okay, but-- but now we do,
and this is not happening.

365
00:22:09.664 --> 00:22:14.044
No, this can't happen.
And this never happened, okay?

366
00:22:15.212 --> 00:22:18.882
Wait. Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

367
00:22:18.965 --> 00:22:20.467
We-- We can-- We can still have--

368
00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:24.346
-Sorry. Sorry.
-Hello. Hi. Sorry.

369
00:22:26.097 --> 00:22:30.477
Listen, we can still have dinner. Okay?
It doesn't have to be a date.

370
00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:32.687
We-- It can just be a funny coincidence

371
00:22:32.771 --> 00:22:37.025
that we both happened to turn up
to the same fabulous restaurant,

372
00:22:37.108 --> 00:22:39.319
both of us alone…

373
00:22:40.737 --> 00:22:42.781
and hungry.

374
00:22:44.699 --> 00:22:45.951
That can happen.

375
00:22:47.327 --> 00:22:48.328
Right?

376
00:22:51.831 --> 00:22:53.375
I mean, I am quite hungry.

377
00:23:31.538 --> 00:23:34.541
…to Lust Conquers All Stars.

378
00:23:34.624 --> 00:23:38.670
Our winning couples from previous seasons
will put their love to the test.

379
00:23:38.753 --> 00:23:41.923
Will it be
last season's winners Ellie and Danthony,

380
00:23:42.757 --> 00:23:44.217
or season one's winners…

381
00:23:44.301 --> 00:23:45.802
Hello, Coach Lasso.

382
00:23:45.886 --> 00:23:50.098
Hey, Doc. So tonight I'm just gonna
keep checking in on you every 20 minutes.

383
00:23:50.181 --> 00:23:51.892
It's standard concussion protocol,

384
00:23:51.975 --> 00:23:54.269
but I'm gonna change my voice
every time I call you

385
00:23:54.352 --> 00:23:55.770
so it stays exciting for you.

386
00:23:55.854 --> 00:23:57.772
Have you been feeling dizzy or nauseous?

387
00:23:59.316 --> 00:24:01.318
That's what it sounds like when you laugh.

388
00:24:02.819 --> 00:24:04.237
I'm fine, Coach Lasso.

389
00:24:05.447 --> 00:24:08.241
Then I'll talk to you in twenty minutes.
Sling Blade.

390
00:24:09.492 --> 00:24:10.619
Hey, Ted…

391
00:24:10.702 --> 00:24:11.995
Yes.

392
00:24:12.621 --> 00:24:15.165
I was scared today. Really scared.

393
00:24:17.459 --> 00:24:20.212
I love riding my bike.
It's my happy place.

394
00:24:20.295 --> 00:24:27.135
And after today, I was worried
I'll be too scared to enjoy riding again.

395
00:24:28.595 --> 00:24:30.639
I would say
that fear's a lot like underwear.

396
00:24:30.722 --> 00:24:34.267
No, I don't want to discuss it.
I don't need a pep talk.

397
00:24:34.935 --> 00:24:37.604
Ted, I just wanted to tell you
how I was feeling.

398
00:24:37.687 --> 00:24:40.106
Well, I appreciate it. Means a lot.

399
00:24:40.690 --> 00:24:42.192
And I'm glad I did it.

400
00:24:42.275 --> 00:24:43.944
Good luck this weekend.

401
00:24:49.366 --> 00:24:50.700
Okay, A-C-M,

402
00:24:50.784 --> 00:24:53.370
I don't know who you are,
but I am coming after your A-S-S.

403
00:24:53.453 --> 00:24:54.454
Let's go.

404
00:24:54.537 --> 00:24:55.538
All right.

405
00:24:57.624 --> 00:24:59.209
Oh, God. It's a bottomless pit.

406
00:24:59.292 --> 00:25:00.794
I commend you.

407
00:25:00.877 --> 00:25:04.047
Usually women use
those small handheld purses on dates.

408
00:25:04.130 --> 00:25:05.715
-What do they call it?
-A clutch.

409
00:25:05.799 --> 00:25:07.217
Clutch.

410
00:25:07.300 --> 00:25:09.844
No, I'd rather dig for dinosaur bones

411
00:25:09.928 --> 00:25:12.556
rather than have one of those bags
you can't fit your phone in.

412
00:25:13.139 --> 00:25:15.308
-There you go.
-And this was not a date.

413
00:25:16.226 --> 00:25:17.227
I know.

414
00:25:18.728 --> 00:25:19.854
So…

415
00:25:22.607 --> 00:25:24.442
can we not do this again sometime?

416
00:25:25.902 --> 00:25:27.821
I'm going in alone.

417
00:25:32.492 --> 00:25:33.493
Okay.

418
00:25:44.629 --> 00:25:47.507
No, no. Nev-- never again, Sam.

419
00:25:48.758 --> 00:25:49.759
I mean it.

420
00:25:52.053 --> 00:25:53.054
I have to mean it.

421
00:25:54.180 --> 00:25:56.433
Yeah, yeah, of course. You're right.

422
00:25:57.767 --> 00:26:00.520
-Besides, we have a big game on Sunday.
-Right.

423
00:26:00.604 --> 00:26:02.480
We both need our rest.

424
00:26:02.564 --> 00:26:03.773
Yep.

425
00:26:04.816 --> 00:26:05.817
Good.

426
00:26:10.155 --> 00:26:11.656
-Good night.
-Thank you.

427
00:26:16.328 --> 00:26:17.329
Oh, bloody hell.

428
00:26:19.956 --> 00:26:21.166
Bloody hell.

429
00:27:07.045 --> 00:27:08.547
Gentlemen. Focus up.

430
00:27:10.298 --> 00:27:12.551
All right, fellas,
I want you to close your eyes.

431
00:27:13.260 --> 00:27:14.469
Look around.

432
00:27:15.303 --> 00:27:18.723
You know.
I mean, open them up and take it all in.

433
00:27:19.516 --> 00:27:25.689
But remember, this right behind me,
just a regular old football pitch.

434
00:27:26.273 --> 00:27:28.358
You take away the stadium
and all the stands,

435
00:27:28.441 --> 00:27:33.071
I think you'll find it's the same size
as our pitch back home on Nelson Road.

436
00:27:33.154 --> 00:27:35.073
-Not exactly.
-What's that?

437
00:27:35.156 --> 00:27:36.866
It's 500 square yards bigger.

438
00:27:36.950 --> 00:27:39.369
-Really? The pitches aren't the same size?
-No.

439
00:27:39.452 --> 00:27:42.247
-This is the biggest pitch in the country.
-Huge advantage for City.

440
00:27:42.330 --> 00:27:46.668
Boy, oh, boy. This sport has
the loosiest-goosiest rules of all.

441
00:27:46.751 --> 00:27:48.253
Tough to get my head around sometimes.
Okay.

442
00:27:48.336 --> 00:27:50.589
All right. It's bigger.

443
00:27:50.672 --> 00:27:54.092
And, look, I know y'all grew up
watching games on this field,

444
00:27:54.175 --> 00:27:56.052
so you're probably a little nervous.

445
00:27:56.136 --> 00:27:57.721
Shoot, I know I got goose bumps.

446
00:27:58.305 --> 00:28:00.599
I remember being a little kid,
sitting in front of the television

447
00:28:00.682 --> 00:28:03.685
and watching Queen perform
right over there during Live Aid.

448
00:28:03.768 --> 00:28:05.645
-No, you didn't.
-That was old Wembley.

449
00:28:05.729 --> 00:28:07.439
That field was even bigger.

450
00:28:07.522 --> 00:28:08.523
It doesn't matter.

451
00:28:08.607 --> 00:28:13.111
Point is, guys, we're here now, okay?

452
00:28:13.194 --> 00:28:14.195
At this Wembley.

453
00:28:15.363 --> 00:28:17.699
The one that Freddie Mercury
never stepped foot in.

454
00:28:18.366 --> 00:28:20.160
And this is our day to make history.

455
00:28:20.577 --> 00:28:22.287
And I believe we're gonna do just that.

456
00:28:22.787 --> 00:28:25.957
Go ahead, take one more glance,
then let's head back in.

457
00:28:26.041 --> 00:28:27.042
We got work to do.

458
00:28:40.263 --> 00:28:42.807
Richmond!

459
00:29:01.409 --> 00:29:02.744
City! City!

460
00:29:04.871 --> 00:29:06.998
-City!
-City!

461
00:29:07.082 --> 00:29:08.792
Yes! Come on!

462
00:29:09.751 --> 00:29:11.002
Look at this. Not bad, is it?

463
00:29:11.086 --> 00:29:14.381
Well, well, well.
Hey, these are bang tidy seats these, man.

464
00:29:14.464 --> 00:29:17.509
That's what you get
when your son's playing in the semifinals.

465
00:29:18.093 --> 00:29:21.513
It's not for the right fucking team,
but what can you do, eh?

466
00:29:21.596 --> 00:29:23.557
Here you are. Get on that, kiddo.

467
00:29:25.684 --> 00:29:28.353
We win this match,
we get Richmond tattoos.

468
00:29:28.436 --> 00:29:29.437
Already got one.

469
00:29:30.230 --> 00:29:32.691
-Where?
-Mind your fucking business.

470
00:29:34.192 --> 00:29:35.860
I'm just not sure how this can…

471
00:29:35.944 --> 00:29:37.654
What about if they have
the game of their lives?

472
00:29:37.737 --> 00:29:39.531
Oh, yeah. I was hoping for that.

473
00:29:46.121 --> 00:29:47.122
You good, Coach?

474
00:29:48.832 --> 00:29:50.041
Oh, yeah.

475
00:29:50.125 --> 00:29:54.254
I'm just doing some breathing exercises
that Doc taught me, that's all.

476
00:29:54.754 --> 00:29:56.715
Hope it's not stomach problems again.

477
00:29:56.798 --> 00:29:59.009
Tell me you didn't eat the prawn cocktail.

478
00:29:59.092 --> 00:30:00.093
No, never.

479
00:30:02.053 --> 00:30:03.305
Guys, it's time.

480
00:30:05.348 --> 00:30:07.142
Here we go. Come on.

481
00:30:08.685 --> 00:30:10.645
Hey, fellas, hold on a sec.

482
00:30:10.729 --> 00:30:13.023
I need to tell you all something.

483
00:30:14.357 --> 00:30:15.859
When I left the match against Tottenham,

484
00:30:15.942 --> 00:30:19.654
it-- it wasn't 'cause, you know,
my stomach was bothering me.

485
00:30:21.239 --> 00:30:23.199
It was 'cause I had a panic attack.

486
00:30:27.120 --> 00:30:29.456
I've been having them
from time to time as of late,

487
00:30:29.539 --> 00:30:30.540
and I'm working on it.

488
00:30:31.249 --> 00:30:34.252
But I just want you all to know the truth.

489
00:30:37.047 --> 00:30:38.048
We good?

490
00:30:38.131 --> 00:30:40.383
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah. Of course.

491
00:30:40.467 --> 00:30:42.719
Okay. Okay, all right.
All right, let's go get 'em.

492
00:30:44.346 --> 00:30:45.639
-Richmond on three.
-Wait!

493
00:30:49.017 --> 00:30:51.102
I need to confess something too.

494
00:30:53.271 --> 00:30:56.608
I messed up the time zones
on our transfer deadline,

495
00:30:56.691 --> 00:31:00.278
which is why we didn't sign up
that amazing fullback from Brazil.

496
00:31:00.362 --> 00:31:01.404
Oh, my God.

497
00:31:02.030 --> 00:31:03.782
-That's okay.
-Okay.

498
00:31:03.865 --> 00:31:05.158
-Yeah, okay.
-All good.

499
00:31:06.826 --> 00:31:08.787
-Okay.
-That's all right. Yeah.

